      <rdf:Description rdf:about=""
            xmlns:photoshop="http://ns.adobe.com/photoshop/1.0/">
         <photoshop:AuthorsPosition>Kaushik</photoshop:AuthorsPosition>
         <photoshop:CaptionWriter>Anubha Kaushik is professor, former Dean and Chairperson, Department of Environmental Science and Engineering, G.J. University of Science and Technology, Hisar, India. She obtained her doctorate from Kurukshetra University, Kurukshetra and has been teaching ecology and environmental sciences in M.D. University, Rohtak, K.U. Kurukshetra and G.J. University of Science and Technology, Hisar for the last 25 years. She has won 8 gold medals in her academic career and was awarded Dr. B.R. Ambedkar Fellowship Award and Gold Medal and various National Scholarships/Fellowships. She has published a large number of research papers in international and national journals of repute and guided several P.G. and doctoral theses. She is in the editorial board of several international and national journals and reviewer of many international journals of environment. She has organized and participated in many international and national conferences, seminars, workshops and refresher courses and chaired technical sessions in some. She has been a member of Appellate Authority, Haryana, a member of State Steering Committee of National Biodiversity Strategy and Action Plan, Nominee, State Environmental Protection Council, Haryana, Resource Person of United States Educational Foundation in India (USEFI, Fulbright) as International Round Table (SAARC) of Environment and Health, and member of several other prestigious academic and advisory committees of University Grants Commission, All India Radio and various Indian universities. She has visited Canada and several European countries.</photoshop:CaptionWriter>
      </rdf:Description>
